Loadstones are visually almost indistinguishable from the other grey
stones, which indicates that they are the same size as those other grey
stones. Despite this, they have *50 times* the encumbrance value, which
suggests that they would have to be 50 times as dense as the other grey
stones if they were merely naturally heavy.

I would guess that flint is about 4-5 times denser than water (relative
density 1), which points to loadstones being roughly ten times as dense
as the densest materials known (osmium and iridium, both roughly 22.5
times denser than water).

They're magically heavy.

(Also, in the original source material for the luckstone and loadstone,
it's made clear that loadstones are magically heavy as well as being
magically undiscardable.)
